sily implemented. Some changes or reasonably feasible measures? Six-week walkthroughs cross-team... producing matrix. That's some changes, reasonably feasible. Not easy low cost? Might be moderate. Probably 3 = some changes, reasonably feasible measures. Could be 4 = easy to implement at low cost? Inventory and walkthrough maybe moderate cost. I'd say 3.\n\nEvidence: Requires coordination of engineers, researchers, counsel for six weeks but uses existing staff and processes.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree idea preserves/modifies paradigm anchored to problem. Paradigm preserving = standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way unchanged. This is audit, standard compliance. Introduces new elements? It's just assessment. Probably 1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working unchanged.\n\nEvidence: It treats compliance as a conventional gap audit without changing R&D-logging relationship.\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree not only rare but ingenious... Common, mundane, boring =1. Gap audit is common.\n\nEvidence: Gap audits against new regulation are a routine, widely expressed compliance response.\n\nThus scores: applicability 4, effectiveness 3, acceptability 4, implementability 3, paradigm_relatedness 1, originality 1.\n\nProvide output format. Probably JSON? Instruction says return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Could be bullet list.\n\nWe'll produce structured.\n\nLet's ensure one sentence evidence each.\n\nApplicability_evidence: The proposal directly inventories high-risk systems against Article 12 logging mandates to meet the mandate.\nApplicability:4\n\nEffectiveness_evidence: It maps gaps and assigns remediation owners but does not itself install automatic event recording required by Article 12.\nEffectiveness:3\n\nAcceptability_evidence: A documented proactive compliance audit is a common, regulator-expected practice that violates no norms.\nAcceptability:4\n\nImplementability_evidence: Running six-week cross-team walkthroughs with existing staff to produce a compliance matrix is reasonably feasible though not trivial.\nImplementability:3\n\nParadigm_relatedness_evidence: The audit treats compliance as standard logging practice and leaves the lab's R&D workflow unchanged.\nParadigm_relatedness:1\n\nOriginality_evidence: Gap audits for new regulatory articles are a routine, widely expressed response in AI labs.\nOriginality:1\n\nReturn.\n\n",
