fectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution (partial)\n2 = unreasonable or unlikely\n1 = solves unrelated problem\n\nIt directly meets Article 12(1)(2) logging mandate, guarantees compliance. Will solve problem. So 4.\n\nApplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 = solves identified problem directly related\n3 = solves implied problem...\nProposal directly addresses how to meet logging mandate. So 4.\n\nReturn rating with evidence sentence then score.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence first then <subscale>.\n\nProbably JSON? Instruction says return rating echoing its id exactly. Provide subscale_evidence and subscale.\n\nLet's output structured list.\n\nMake one sentence evidence for each.\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: The proposal introduces a reusable middleware/SDK for logging but treats compliance as standard logging practice without redefining the lab's R&D-compliance relationship.\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n\noriginality_evidence: Centralized logging middleware with configurable Annex III fields is a familiar engineering solution rather than an ingenious or surprising approach.\noriginality: 1? Hmm decide. Let's pick 2 as interesting. Might be safer 1 common mundane boring. The description \"Universal Logging Middleware\" sounds common. I think originality = 1 (common, mundane, boring). Let's go with 1.\n\nImplementability_evidence: Building and instrumenting a portfolio-wide SDK requires significant engineering effort across projects but remains feasible within an R&D lab.\nimplementability: 3? Significant change ->2. Might be 2 = significant change expensive/difficult. Let's pick 2? \"some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\" vs \"significant change, or expensive or difficult\". Building plug-in SDK for all high-risk systems is significant. I'd say 2.\n\nAcceptability_evidence: Standardized logging to meet legal traceability requirements violates no norms and aligns with audit expectations.\nacceptability: 4\n\neffectiveness_evidence: The middleware directly enables automatic recording of required events and Annex III fields, solving the mandated logging compliance problem.\neffectiveness: 4\n\napplicability_evidence: The proposal addresses the stated problem of meeting Article 12 logging mandates for the lab's high-risk AI R&D portfolio.\napplicability: 4\n\nReturn.\n\nEnsure order listed: paradigm_relatedness, originality, implementability, acceptability, effectiveness, applicability\n\nProvide id P2960.\n\nLet's output.",
